Task 3: Pinpoint Latency Bottlenecks and Failed Requests
Subtask 3.1: Identify Performance Bottlenecks
Create a service with artificial latency:
cat << EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: slow-service
  namespace: bookinfo-tracing
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: slow-service
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: slow-service
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: slow-service
        image: nginx:alpine
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        command: ["/bin/sh"]
        args: ["-c", "while true; do sleep 2; echo 'Slow response' | nc -l -p 80; done"]
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: slow-service
  namespace: bookinfo-tracing
spec:
  selector:
    app: slow-service
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80
EOF
Modify the productpage to call the slow service:
# This simulates adding a slow dependency
oc patch deployment productpage-v1 -n bookinfo-tracing -p '{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"productpage","env":[{"name":"SLOW_SERVICE_URL","value":"http://slow-service.bookinfo-tracing.svc.cluster.local"}]}]}}}}'
Generate traffic and analyze bottlenecks:
for i in {1..10}; do
  curl -s "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage" > /dev/null
  echo "Request $i with slow dependency sent"
  sleep 1
done
In Jaeger UI, identify bottlenecks:
Look for traces with long durations
Identify spans that take the most time
Use the timeline view to see where time is spent
Check for parallel vs sequential operations
Subtask 3.2: Analyze Failed Requests
Create a service that occasionally fails:
cat << EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: flaky-service
  namespace: bookinfo-tracing
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: flaky-service
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: flaky-service
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: flaky-service
        image: nginx:alpine
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        command: ["/bin/sh"]
        args: ["-c", "while true; do if [ $((RANDOM % 3)) -eq 0 ]; then echo 'HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error' | nc -l -p 80; else echo 'HTTP/1.1 200 OK' | nc -l -p 80; fi; done"]
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: flaky-service
  namespace: bookinfo-tracing
spec:
  selector:
    app: flaky-service
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80
EOF
